{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cf07396bebd8149f2d99cc7c272e2af4b8d03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{35} - 6^{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> is evaluated, the units (ones) digit is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420dcafbb85c5fcaec5012f6869adbb90191f85f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   1  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   9  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   2  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   5  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   6  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"384\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to any power has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to any power has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cf07396bebd8149f2d99cc7c272e2af4b8d03e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{35} - 6^{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> would be the same as the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a200ce05617415766b7470dc6e04fa9e68ceff4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - 6 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, which has a units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d101b8512363c39cbfb972899c37ba2fc5c0feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28modular_arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(modular_arithmetic)\">Solution 2 (modular arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (modular arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The units digit of an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is its remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22463bfe33cdaece746532048ba191f09e2694c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, so we must find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/461496663bcbf0e38eec8a7a7896deba08cd2753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{35} - 6^{21} \\equiv \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c0ef27b6e90ad09d90d9c419a0424f911ac5e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le r \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c567ee6db21d84b9dc166ca382e7e398c7558f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot 5 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f4ae20cb2a82068a8617097e8bce15f78452ff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"20\" />, so in general <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2900526c65002be29d2ba3ab020863c940ac8067.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n} \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d479b103edfd99929c593620dbd00fa634284f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{n} \\equiv 6\\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965ac6a39c0b4d67771c31210b98312ae2e4f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52cfb5227f31958fd30ee84b34755a51189b7b27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{35} - 6^{21} \\equiv 5-6 \\equiv \\textbf{(B)}\\ 9 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 